{"title":"Career Roadmap: Computational Biologist","role":"Computational Biologist","summary":"A Computational Biologist uses computational methods, statistics and biological knowledge to analyze complex biological datasets.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Sc. (Bachelor of Science – General / Honours)","Course":"Bioinformatics"},"about":[{"label":"Primary Goal","text":"Build expertise in biology, programming, statistics, bioinformatics algorithms and computational analysis of biological data"}],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career Roadmap Overview"},{"type":"p","text":"A Computational Biologist uses computational methods, statistics and biological knowledge to analyze complex biological datasets."},{"type":"p","text":"Typical applications include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Genomics"},{"text":"Transcriptomics"},{"text":"Proteomics"},{"text":"Structural biology"},{"text":"Drug discovery"},{"text":"Precision medicine"},{"text":"Systems biology"},{"text":"Population genetics"},{"text":"Single-cell biology"},{"text":"Biological network analysis"}]},{"type":"p","text":"For this career, the strongest profile is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Biology","Programming","Statistics","Algorithms","Bioinformatics","Domain Specialization"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"A B.Sc. Bioinformatics provides a direct foundation, but research-oriented computational biology positions often become substantially more accessible after an M.Sc./M.Tech. and, for advanced research roles, a Ph.D."}]},{"heading":"What to Build During UG","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Year","Build This","Learn From","Proof to Create","Gap to Avoid"],"rows":[[{"text":"1st Year"},{"text":"Biology + programming foundation"},{"text":"Cell biology, genetics, Python"},{"text":"Biology coding portfolio"},{"text":"Learning coding without biology"}],[{"text":"2nd Year"},{"text":"Bioinformatics fundamentals"},{"text":"Genomics,